{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Rochester Dragons were a men's ultimate team based in Rochester, New York, competing in the East Division of the American Ultimate Disc League.","title":"Rochester Dragons"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The team was introduced during the 2012 season as the Buffalo Hunters before moving to Rochester in 2013.","title":"Rochester Dragons"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The Dragons played their 2014 home games at SUNY Brockport in Brockport, New York with the exception of the May 17, 2014 game which was played at Sahlen's Stadium in Rochester, New York, known for being the home of the 2015 USL Champion Rochester Rhinos and the Western New York Flash.","title":"Rochester Dragons"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The 2015 home games are scheduled to be played at Spencerport High School's stadium.","title":"Rochester Dragons"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The Dragons had their first franchise win on May 5, 2013 against the New Jersey Hammerheads, winning 26 to 14 at home.","title":"Rochester Dragons"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Jordan Leigh Angeli (born May 31, 1986) is an American former soccer player from Lakewood, Colorado.","title":"Jordan Angeli"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She last played for the Western New York Flash in the National Women's Soccer League after a preseason trade with the Washington Spirit.","title":"Jordan Angeli"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Known for her versatility, Angeli originally debuted for the Santa Clara University women's soccer team as a defender, was moved to forward for Santa Clara in 2005, and played as a midfielder for the United States U-20 women's national soccer team at the 2006 FIFA U-20 Women's World Championship.","title":"Jordan Angeli"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Capelli Sport Stadium, formerly PAETEC Park, Marina Auto Stadium, Rochester Rhinos Stadium, and Sahlen's Stadium, is a soccer-specific stadium in Rochester, New York, US.","title":"Capelli Sport Stadium"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is home to the Rochester Rhinos of the United Soccer League and the Rochester Rattlers of Major League Lacrosse.","title":"Capelli Sport Stadium"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It was also home of the Western New York Flash of the National Women's Soccer League.","title":"Capelli Sport Stadium"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The stadium hosts other sporting events such as collegiate soccer, Rochester Rhinos Elite youth soccer games and practices, American football, field hockey and drum and bugle corps competitions as well as concerts.","title":"Capelli Sport Stadium"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Victoria Teresa DiMartino (born September 4, 1991) is an American soccer player from Massapequa, New York.","title":"Vicki DiMartino"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" She is a forward for the Western New York Flash in the National Women's Soccer League, and a defender for the United States U-20 women's national soccer team.","title":"Vicki DiMartino"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The 2016 season was Western New York Flash's ninth season, the fourth in which they competed in the National Women's Soccer League, the top division of women's soccer in the United States.","title":"2016 Western New York Flash season"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The season ended with the Flash's first finals appearance since the 2013 NWSL season and the franchise's first NWSL Championship victory.","title":"2016 Western New York Flash season"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It was also the final season of the NWSL franchise's existence in Rochester, New York, or as the Western New York Flash, after being purchased by the North Carolina FC organization, moved to Cary, North Carolina, and rebranded as the North Carolina Courage in January 2017.","title":"2016 Western New York Flash season"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" It was replaced in March 2017 by a new Buffalo-based Western New York Flash team in United Women's Soccer.","title":"2016 Western New York Flash season"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The 2010 season was Buffalo Flash's second season of existence, and the second in which they competed in the W-League, at the time the second division of women's soccer in the United States.","title":"2010 Buffalo Flash season"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" This was the last year the Flash operated under the Buffalo name, they became the Western New York Flash when they moved on to Women's Professional Soccer in 2011.","title":"2010 Buffalo Flash season"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Massapequa, New York
